  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in House",
    "asOf": "2026-06-25",
    "date": "2026-11-17T21:21:52Z",
    "text": "Securing Access to Care for Seniors in Critical Condition Act of 2025\n\nThis bill exempts additional types of hospital stays from the Medicare site-neutral payment rate for long-term care hospitals (LTCHs) and extends certain adjustments to the payment rate. (The site-neutral rate is the lower of Medicare\u2019s acute care hospital payment rate under the inpatient prospective payment system or 100% of the cost of the stay. LTCH stays that do not qualify for the specialized LTCH payment rate under Medicare are instead paid at the lower, site-neutral rate.)\n\nSpecifically, the bill exempts discharges from LTCHs from the site-neutral payment rate if the discharge meets specified high acuity criteria. It also allows discharges to qualify for the exemption if certain intensive care or ventilator services were furnished by a critical access hospital immediately prior to the LTCH stay. These exemptions apply to discharges that occur on or after October 1, 2026.\n\nThe bill additionally extends an adjustment that reduces the site-neutral payment rate through FY2032."
  },
